WEBVTT

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:03.940
If you're a man, then stand up to the punches without running away, huh...

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.080
Sorry, Dad...

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:17.300
You'll have to wait for me some more before we can go fishing together.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.620
Tetsukado!

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:20.950
It went in!

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:31.570
The withdrawal exam, an option that had never existed before, finished with everyone resolving their conflict during the PK match.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:33.950
In the end, no one dropped out of the team.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.000
Aw, she missed.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.070
No, don't go that way!

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.950
Let's begin the running drills!

00:00:58.670 --> 00:00:59.750
Ready!

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:03.500
Ready!

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.540
That's it, keep it up!

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:10.970
Don't forget that timing!

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:29.980
I don't need your help.

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:33.690
I only do what is within my ability to win.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:42.580
Don't mind him.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:44.820
Right, Captain?

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:46.470
Yeah...

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:31.510
Here is the information for our next opponent, Australia's Big Waves.

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:36.120
According to the data, their average score per match is 7.67.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.820
They always win by a wide point margin.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.570
So they're a team that possesses outstanding offense.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.220
The issue would be how we can defend against them.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.500
Data only consists of numbers.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:50.750
Once we have an actual match with them, I'll uncover their weak spot.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.620
By then, it'll be too late.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:57.850
In addition...

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:01.880
Sakura-chan, your parents are here to visit.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.390
You didn't have to come all this way to see how I was doing.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.700
Don't blame us for worrying.

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:14.250
Not after how you suddenly insisted that you would be playing soccer.

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:18.480
But you've won the first match, at least.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.440
It'll be fine. I'm doing my best.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:24.750
We'll be cheering for you at the stands in the next match.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:27.700
The world has its attention on you.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:31.370
As a representative of Japan, don't show any embarrassing plays.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:31.870
Okay.

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:44.620
We're blessed with fine weather today here at Holy Road Stadium!

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:54.970
The match between Japan's Inazuma Japan and Australia's Big Waves in FFI Vision 2's Asia district preliminaries is about to begin!

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:58.150
Hayato-niichan will be doing lots this match too, right?

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:00.400
Of course! He's the best on the team!

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:06.970
Here I go!

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:13.120
Give me a quicker pass!

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:16.670
Okay then, here it comes!

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:21.550
Nice! Good reaction!

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:28.850
Sorry...

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:31.600
No, it's okay.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:35.060
Useless girl.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:37.670
Huh?

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:43.020
Minaho-kun, position yourself at an angle of 25 degrees!

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:45.150
I am not a protractor!

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:52.080
At least they look useful.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.000
Come on!

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.400
Did you see that?

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:06.340
I won't let anyone score a goal through me anymore!

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.900
We'll see how it turns out in a real game.

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:12.510
You just leave the goal to me!

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:23.020
You guys understand why we've traveled all this way here to fight?

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:24.020
Yes, sir.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.420
Good. Then win at all costs.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:27.500
Yeah!

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:31.500
The time has come.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:32.420
Yeah.

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:34.370
Our future depends on this.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:37.270
Losing is not an option.

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:45.200
The match between Big Waves and Inazuma Japan, the winners of the first match, will now begin!

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:54.680
Shindou, you're too far back!

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:56.120
I'll be fine here.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:02.100
We already have a good grasp of your fighting technique!

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:03.940
You watched the Fire Dragon match, huh?

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.900
We will most definitely beat you!

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:10.400
They're tough!

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:16.950
A fierce clash right off the bat!

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:22.620
Inazuma Japan moved rather slowly in their first game, and even today, they are under pressure!

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:41.600
Once more!

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:47.650
I can't do it!

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:49.850
There's no time for tears.

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:50.740
Continue.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:53.050
You are going to be best in the world.

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:58.240
Best in the world...

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:10.060
Over here!

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:17.680
Oh dear, that was a pass miss!

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:23.480
No way!

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:24.340
Wow!

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.220
What? What was that?

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:27.520
She's pretty cool!

00:08:27.970 --> 00:08:31.480
Nozaki saves them from danger with her exceptional balance!

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:34.600
They are being pushed back, as I expected.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.750
But they've all improved tremendously!

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:39.750
Let's hope so.

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:43.700
Captain!

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:44.450
Okay!

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:48.920
I have to make use of this team somehow, if we want to win!

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:51.410
Tenma!

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:53.220
Okay!

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:58.020
God's Baton!

00:08:59.100 --> 00:08:59.460
Nozaki!

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:00.800
Eh, me?

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:01.870
Run!

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:03.050
O-Okay!

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:04.430
Kusaka!

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:12.180
Matatagi!

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:13.810
Over here!

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:14.950
Okay!

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:20.450
Bicycle Sword!

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:24.080
What?

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:29.320
Tsurugi's new hissatsu shoot soars in!

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:31.040
Inazuma Japan scores the first goal!

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:33.040
When did you come up with a new hissatsu?!

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:36.200
All right, all right!

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.340
Nii-chan's pass made it to the goal!

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:41.150
We got God's Baton to work!

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:41.810
Yeah.

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:45.520
We can win this!

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:46.420
Yeah.

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:49.300
Let's all play an active role in this together!

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:50.770
They did it!

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:52.180
We scored the first point!

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:05.770
I'll stop you!

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:11.090
Wonder Trap!

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:13.590
Shindou-san!

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:15.460
Kusaka!

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:17.720
Yo!

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:20.340
Now!

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:23.060
Hissatsu tactics!

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:23.890
Suck Out!

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:24.970
Yeah!

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:37.900
W-What the hell?

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:44.450
Big Waves' hissatsu tactics trumps God's Baton!

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:45.320
What?

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.780
Those movements of theirs are interesting.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:52.540
It was Shindou's mistake for showing his hand first.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:57.420
You can't stop me!

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:01.450
He breaks past Inazuma Japan's final line of defense!

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:03.300
Will he end up scoring the goal?!

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:05.140
I'll stop them!

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:11.100
He still doesn't trust me?!

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:15.160
Nozaki!

00:11:17.270 --> 00:11:18.110
Matatagi!

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:23.240
Suck Out!

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:24.160
Yeah!

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:35.420
Nii-chan!

00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:38.720
No matter how hard you try, it'll be the same.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:40.970
The ball is stolen from Matatagi!

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:43.220
God's Baton fails again!

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:48.660
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:54.450
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:11:57.050 --> 00:11:59.850
Inazuma Japan goes into offense once again!

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:03.200
Tenma!

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:05.570
Okay!

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:06.800
Pass it to Tsurugi!

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:08.870
Suck Out!

00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:13.820
I won't let you!

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:25.570
That defense renders useless all of our offense.

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:28.560
Yeah, it's like we're fighting with the ocean.

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:30.980
But that's strange.

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:35.190
Aren't they supposed to be a team with outstanding offense?

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:39.650
Now that you mention it, their play style is completely different from the data.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:44.570
Was the data we got wrong?

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:49.790
Whatever the case, we can't use God's Baton anymore.

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:52.250
Oh no...

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:55.500
An exciting game at its climax!

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.070
The score is 1-0 with Inazuma Japan in the lead!

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:02.250
But now that Big Waves has stopped God's Baton, how will they counterattack?!

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:04.170
I won't let you pass!

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:05.250
Too weak.

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:07.010
Cole!

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:09.270
Big Waves makes a swift attack!

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:11.680
Cole stands freely before Japan's goal!

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:13.430
We can't lose any points.

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:15.390
I'll stop him no matter what!

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:18.360
Again!

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:20.210
Move, Shindou!

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:21.560
You're blocking my view!

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:24.060
Oh no!

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:25.320
Come on!

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:27.460
Megalodon!

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:33.740
I'm the goalkeeper here!

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:40.500
Goal!

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:41.380
Yes!

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:45.470
Cole's hissatsu shoot Megalodon goes in!

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:47.360
Big Waves makes a tie!

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:52.220
Now do you see?

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:54.740
Practice isn't the same as the real thing.

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:01.800
Not much time remains for the first half!

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:05.200
Will it remain a tie or will the scales tip in one team's favor?!

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:22.420
Minaho-kun, pass to the left at 45 degrees!

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:25.270
Your instructions are too detailed!

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:27.090
Oh, come on...

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:28.570
I'll fix it on my end!

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:32.390
I can't see the ball!

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.220
He missed getting the ball!

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:35.890
Let me handle it!

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:45.150
There's Nozaki's magnificent dance, negating Manabe's error!

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:50.900
Morimura!

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:52.650
Okay!

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:01.740
Are you okay?

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:06.500
It wasn't on purpose.

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:07.460
Okay?

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:21.060
Nozaki makes another nice cover!

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:22.730
Did you see that?

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:24.250
Yeah, it's just awful.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:27.070
That girl hasn't changed at all.

00:15:29.730 --> 00:15:31.500
The first half is over!

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:35.080
Both teams move forward and back without giving way!

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:42.500
Now everyone will have a high opinion of me.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:46.770
What's wrong?

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:56.250
She should be able to respond faster with her reaction time, so I was wondering why her plays are always at the last minute.

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:59.270
Perhaps there is a reason for it.

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:05.020
Are you okay?

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:05.840
Yeah.

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:10.850
I'm sorry about earlier.

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:20.620
I don't want to believe it, but you didn't do that on purpose, did you?

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.280
Don't be silly!

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:26.350
But when you get involved, Nozaki, everything gets messed up.

00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:27.440
Yeah.

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:31.160
The rhythm of our offense gets cut off, or our chances turn into close calls.

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:33.270
The results end in ways beyond my calculations.

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:35.550
Why won't it go well, I wonder?

00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:40.640
I don't know anything! I only want to bring results for the team!

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:45.350
If I don't...

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:49.150
Then I'll have to relive those bad memories again...

00:16:52.170 --> 00:16:54.000
The second half begins!

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:01.700
You can do it, Sakura!

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:04.080
Show the world what you can do!

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:10.500
Matatagi!

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:14.260
What?

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:15.050
Sakura?

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:16.500
I have to show them my good side!

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:21.720
The ball is stolen from Sakura!

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:24.680
Big Waves makes a counterattack from the sides!

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:35.100
Don't move too far from your position.

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:50.530
Who do I pass it to...?

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:53.300
Nozaki!

00:17:53.770 --> 00:17:54.540
Leave it to me!

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:01.890
Those guys were after Nozaki-san all along!

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:03.560
Shindou-san!

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:08.640
That was the perfect assist for Big Waves!

00:18:10.950 --> 00:18:11.560
What?!

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:14.250
Megalodon!

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:20.360
I'll stop it this time!

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:31.080
It's in!

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:33.590
Big Waves takes the lead!

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:36.490
Hey!

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:39.620
What did you pass to the other team for?!

00:18:39.620 --> 00:18:41.610
B-But I didn't mean...

00:18:41.610 --> 00:18:44.420
You aren't mistaking whose team you're on, are you?

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:47.570
I was just...

00:18:55.770 --> 00:18:56.850
What's wrong?

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:00.210
Soccer is supposed to be fun...

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:02.730
But you look miserable.

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:06.530
What are you talking about, Captain?

00:19:06.530 --> 00:19:08.700
Do I look miserable to you right now?

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:13.330
If it's just my imagination, then never mind.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:31.970
What went wrong in your performance today?

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:34.360
I know you could've done better than her.

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:38.150
Let's not hang up this medal.

00:19:41.420 --> 00:19:44.990
I am <i>not</i>  feeling miserable at all!

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:47.550
You're full of openings!

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:50.550
What's the matter, Nozaki?!

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:52.490
She loses the ball again!

00:19:55.150 --> 00:19:55.580
Cole!

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:57.340
We'll bring them down!

00:19:57.680 --> 00:19:58.540
I'll stop you!

00:20:00.370 --> 00:20:02.570
The likes of you can't stop us!

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:07.320
That was a conclusive move!

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:11.070
Will Inazuma Japan end up allowing them another goal?!

00:20:11.870 --> 00:20:12.520
Shindou...

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:16.300
Megalodon!

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:22.690
It's <i>me</i>  who will protect the goal!

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:28.120
Wild Dunk!

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:31.970
He did it!

00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:32.610
Ibuki!

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:34.720
Yes!

00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:35.870
He blocks it!

00:20:35.870 --> 00:20:43.170
Inazuma Japan's goalkeeper Ibuki stops Big Waves from earning another goal with his hissatsu Wild Dunk!

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:46.420
Check that out! Did you see that, Shindou?!

00:20:47.670 --> 00:20:49.470
That's what the goalkeeper should be doing.

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:54.700
That was incredible!

00:20:55.700 --> 00:20:59.720
Looks like I will have to update your personal data.

00:20:59.720 --> 00:21:02.940
I knew you had it in you.

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:06.570
Ibuki!

00:21:07.520 --> 00:21:09.490
Our goal is in your hands, goalkeeper!

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:13.860
Yeah!

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:18.000
A hissatsu technique, huh...

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:21.670
Just watch! I can do it too!

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:26.000
If this keeps up, I...

00:22:54.660 --> 00:22:58.420
Sakura faces her parents and herself.

00:22:58.600 --> 00:23:01.350
Sakura, let's win this together!

00:23:01.570 --> 00:23:03.900
Next, Let's Play Fun Soccer!

00:23:04.150 --> 00:23:06.100
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.170 --> 00:23:19.350
The Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy's proverb today is...

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:25.770
I do what is within my ability to win!

00:23:26.060 --> 00:23:26.850
That's all!
